  "physical": "A native motor choice drives sustained left/right pulses in the existing mixture body. Its actual contact supplies side plus signed taste to native sensory ports; all silent contacts retain side while forcing physical writes off. Movement-step states stay in the body adapter.",
  "laws": "Single-pair profiles fully cross independent A/B binary laws and both mark laws per root. The three-pair stress crosses all 8 A maps with both mark laws and sets B to the inverse for each pair. C has newly drawn odors and unrelated laws. Flipped keeps its prime sensory streams and inverts only earlier A taste. B-only substitutes B for A while holding length constant. Donor signs share neither private law nor choices with the receiver, and appear at the receiver's actual receipt event.",
  "scoring": "A, B and marks are measured in distinct silent physical forks of the same pre-probe snapshot. The randomly ordered silent sequence is retained as a secondary measurement. Missed contacts count as incorrect. Joint A and B means both forked physical contacts were correct. The reversal's natural row exposes feedback immediately after each of the first four changed requests; aligned rows mask the earlier changes so all doses share the final physical layout.",
